#: includes/modules/docs.php:45
msgid "Your security overview: the current protection status, activity from the last 7 days, recent events and the result of the most recent scan."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:47
msgid "Summarises which protections are on and which are still off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:48
msgid "Charts blocked requests, failed logins and bans over the last 7 days."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:49
msgid "Lists the newest activity-log events so problems surface early."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:50
msgid "Shows when the site was last scanned and what the scan found."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:53
msgid "Open Modules and turn on the feature areas this site needs — everything else stays dormant."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:54
msgid "Work through Firewall, Login Security and Scanner first; they cover the most common attacks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:55
msgid "Set an alert address in Settings → Alerts & notifications so you hear about incidents without logging in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:56
msgid "Run a first scan from the Scanner page to get a clean baseline to compare against later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:59
msgid "Counters only cover events recorded while the relevant module was active."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:60
msgid "A quiet dashboard is not proof of safety — check the Scanner and Logs pages periodically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:65
msgid "Turn feature areas on or off. A module that is off loads no code, registers no REST routes and shows no menu entry, so unused features cost nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:67
msgid "Activation is the coarse gate; the individual settings inside a module stay as fine-grained switches."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:68
msgid "Turning a module off immediately removes its page from both the plugin nav and the WordPress menu."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:69
msgid "Core modules (Dashboard, Modules, Logs, Settings) are always on and cannot be turned off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:70
msgid "Pro modules show as locked until the Pro add-on is active; then they toggle like any other module."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:73
msgid "Switch on a module to reveal its page, then open that page and configure it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:74
msgid "Leave modules you do not use switched off — it keeps the menu short and skips their code entirely."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:77
msgid "Turning a module off does not erase its settings; switching it back on restores them exactly as they were."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:78
msgid "On upgrade, activation was derived from your existing settings, so a module whose features were all off may start hidden."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:83
msgid "A tamper-evident audit trail of everything that matters: logins, user and role changes, plugin and theme activity, settings changes, blocks and bans."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:85
msgid "Records security-relevant events with actor, IP, severity and timestamp."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:86
msgid "Lets you choose which activity is recorded — user accounts, plugins and themes, settings changes, content — while security events are always logged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:87
msgid "Filters by severity, event type, user or IP, and exports the result as CSV."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:88
msgid "Sends real-time alerts for events above the severity you choose."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:89
msgid "Pro: hash-chains each entry so deleted or edited rows can be detected, and can forward events to a SIEM or syslog collector."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:92
msgid "Set how long entries are kept in Settings → General (log retention, in days)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:93
msgid "Use \"What gets logged\" at the top of this page to switch off any source you do not need — content is the noisiest on an active site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:94
msgid "Choose an alert channel and minimum severity on the Notifications page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:95
msgid "Pro: enable the hash chain in Settings → Compliance & SIEM, then use Verify to prove the log is intact."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:98
msgid "Retention trims old rows on a schedule — set it long enough to cover an investigation, short enough to keep the table small."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:99
msgid "Log verification only proves the chain from the point you enabled it, not events recorded before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:104
msgid "Where alerts go, what raises one, and the mail that arrives on a schedule. Every module feeds into this page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:106
msgid "Delivery: one security email address and one set of channels — Slack, Telegram or a generic webhook — used by every alert, report and failure notice the plugin sends, with a minimum-severity filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:107
msgid "Triggers: every event a module can alert on, in one list — administrator sign-ins, new devices, rogue and hidden administrators, and application passwords."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:108
msgid "Scheduled: a morning report listing every administrator and active plugin with anything that changed since yesterday, a weekly digest, and the daily security scan that finds most of it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:111
msgid "Set the security email once — monitoring warnings, admin alerts and the daily report all use it. Then set the minimum severity so routine noise stays out of your inbox."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:112
msgid "Work down \"What you get told about\" and switch off anything you do not want to hear. A trigger whose module is switched off is not listed at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:113
msgid "Turn on the daily report to get a morning inventory of administrators and active plugins, with new ones called out — then use \"Send a report now\" to see what it looks like."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:116
msgid "Alerts are only as reliable as your site mail. If WordPress email is unreliable here, use Slack, Telegram or a webhook instead — use \"Send a test email\" to find out before an incident does."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:117
msgid "Each trigger also appears on the page of the module that raises it. Both write the same setting, so the two views can never disagree."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:118
msgid "Turning a trigger off does not stop the event being recorded — it is still in the activity log on the Logs page, you just are not mailed about it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:119
msgid "Deactivating GemSecurity emails the alert address with a critical warning naming who did it, and pushes the same message to Slack, Telegram or your webhook — switching security off is the first move in most intrusions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:120
msgid "Every email names the site and its domain in the subject, after an emoji for the event type — so alerts from several installs stay apart in one inbox."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:121
msgid "The first daily report has no baseline, so it lists the inventory without claiming everything is new. Comparisons start the next morning."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:126
msgid "Plugin-wide preferences: log retention, compliance and SIEM forwarding, maintenance lockdown, and settings import/export."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:128
msgid "Compliance: log hash-chaining, SIEM/syslog forwarding and a severity floor for what gets shipped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:129
msgid "Maintenance: site lockdown with a custom message, and (with the GemBackup plugin) taking a backup before plugin or theme updates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:130
msgid "Settings import/export (Pro): move a whole configuration, including which modules are on, between sites."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:133
msgid "Set log retention to suit the site — a busy install fills the log quickly, and 0 keeps entries forever."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:134
msgid "Use lockdown while you investigate an incident: visitors see your message, administrators keep full access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:137
msgid "Alerts, the daily report and the weekly digest are configured on the Notifications page, not here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:138
msgid "What gets written to the activity log is configured on the Logs page, not here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:139
msgid "Lockdown blocks the front end for visitors — remember to switch it back off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:148
msgid "The front door: an IP blocklist, the request firewall and its rules, rate limiting, bot control, the classic WordPress hardening switches, browser security headers and a security.txt file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:150
msgid "Blocks individual IPs and CIDR ranges before WordPress does any real work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:151
msgid "Inspects requests for SQL injection, XSS, path traversal and remote code execution, and can also inspect POST bodies."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:152
msgid "Rate limits front-end requests per IP and throttles 404 floods from vulnerability scanners."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:153
msgid "Hardening: disable XML-RPC, disable the theme/plugin file editor, hide the WordPress version."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:154
msgid "Username enumeration: block ?author=N scans, hide the REST users endpoint and return one generic login error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:155
msgid "Sends security headers — X-Frame-Options, nosniff, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, HSTS and CSP — and collects CSP violation reports."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:156
msgid "Bot control: block known-bad scanners and empty user agents, block AI crawlers, and verify self-declared search engines by reverse DNS so fake Googlebots are turned away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:157
msgid "Publishes /.well-known/security.txt and audits file permissions for world-writable paths."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:158
msgid "With Pro, the hardening pack adds an admin IP allowlist, sensitive-file blocking, no PHP execution in uploads and forced HTTPS."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:161
msgid "Turn the firewall on, then enable the hardening switches one at a time and check the site still works after each."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:162
msgid "Turn the WAF on and leave the four rule families enabled; add POST body inspection only if you can watch for false positives on your own forms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:163
msgid "Only enable the admin IP allowlist if your address is static, and add it before saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:164
msgid "If the site sits behind Cloudflare or another proxy, enable the matching option under Real visitor IP detection — otherwise every visitor looks like the proxy and blocks or rate limits hit everyone at once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:165
msgid "Enable security headers, leave CSP in report-only mode, then read Recent CSP violations for a few days before enforcing it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:166
msgid "Fill in a contact address under security.txt so researchers know where to report problems."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:169
msgid "Disabling XML-RPC breaks the classic WordPress mobile app, Jetpack-style remote publishing and some pingback workflows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:170
msgid "HSTS tells browsers to refuse plain HTTP for the max-age you set — only enable it once HTTPS works on every subdomain you include, and treat preload as permanent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:171
msgid "A CSP that is enforced too early will silently break embeds, analytics and page builders. Report-only first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:172
msgid "Never trust proxy headers unless the site really is behind that proxy — spoofed headers would let an attacker rotate their apparent IP at will."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:173
msgid "A dynamic home IP plus an admin IP allowlist means locking yourself out the next time your router reconnects."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:174
msgid "Comment controls live on the Anti-Spam page, and application passwords on API & Access."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:179
msgid "Every comment and registration control in one place: close comments entirely, or stop spam with invisible bot checks, an optional CAPTCHA and a heuristic score for anything that gets through."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:181
msgid "Closes comments and pingbacks site-wide if the site does not use them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:182
msgid "Adds a hidden honeypot field and a minimum time-to-submit, both invisible to real visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:183
msgid "Optionally adds the CAPTCHA configured on the CAPTCHA page to the comment form as well."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:184
msgid "Scores comments on link count and keyword matches, holding or rejecting the worst."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:187
msgid "If the site does not take comments, disable them entirely — nothing else on this page then matters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:188
msgid "Otherwise turn on silent bot protection — no keys or accounts needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:189
msgid "Leave the minimum submit time at a few seconds; raise it only if spam still gets through."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:190
msgid "Enable heuristic filtering, set the maximum number of links you consider normal, and add keywords you keep seeing in spam."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:193
msgid "Aggressive keyword lists cause false positives — check the held queue for a while after adding new terms."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:194
msgid "Heavily cached sites can serve a stale form timestamp; if legitimate comments are refused, lower the minimum submit time."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:195
msgid "The silent checks stop nearly all automated spam on their own. Add the comment CAPTCHA only if they are not enough — it costs every real visitor a puzzle."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:200
msgid "Active defence: a request firewall that inspects traffic for attack patterns, rate limits and 404 throttling, escalating auto-bans, and live traffic visibility."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:202
msgid "Inspects requests for SQL injection, XSS, local file inclusion and remote code execution patterns, optionally including the request body."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:203
msgid "Rate limits requests and throttles 404 floods — the usual signature of a vulnerability scanner."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:204
msgid "Blocks known-bad bots, empty user agents and your own custom patterns."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:205
msgid "Escalates repeat offenders from strikes to a temporary ban and then a permanent one, all in a ban ledger you can edit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:206
msgid "Detects request anomalies and credential-stuffing bursts, and shows requests as they arrive in Live traffic."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:209
msgid "Enable the firewall and leave all four attack classes on unless a legitimate integration trips one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:210
msgid "Enable the early-load loader so banned requests are rejected before other plugins run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:211
msgid "Set the auto-ban threshold, window and duration to match your traffic — start lenient and tighten later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/modules/docs.php:212
